{"paper": "RRB-GroupD-29-Dec-2025-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 22, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Preeti, Qadir and Reena invest sum in the ratio 2 : 8 : 13, respectively. If they earned total profit of ₹87,193 at the end of year, then what is the positive difference between share of Preeti and Reena?4910", "options": [{"text": "₹41,703", "added": false}, {"text": "₹41,701", "added": false}, {"text": "₹41,702", "added": false}, {"text": "₹41,704", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "partnership", "key_answer": "₹41,701"}, {"n": 2, "text": "The mode of the observations 21, 32, 34, 34, 34, 20, 32, 24, 34, 34, 20, 25, 29, 26 and 20 is:4287", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "mean-median-mode", "key_answer": "34"}, {"n": 3, "text": "Ravi bought a watch for ₹4,800, spent ₹200 on its repair, and sold it for ₹6,000. What is his profit percentage?", "options": [{"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "27%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "22%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": "25 hours"}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "65%", "added": false}, {"text": "100%", "added": false}, {"text": "50%", "added": false}, {"text": "60%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "50%"}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": "4%"}, {"n": 6, "text": "₹8,200 is divided among A, B and C in such a way that if ₹19, ₹9 and ₹13 are deducted from their respective shares, they have money in the ratio 12:19:10. Find the difference between B’s and C’s original shares.", "options": [{"text": "₹1,787", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,841", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,691", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,641", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "2"}, {"n": 7, "text": "The mode of the observations 21, 32, 34, 34, 34, 20, 32, 24, 34, 34, 20, 25, 29, 26 and 20 is:4287", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "20%"}, {"n": 8, "text": "The amount on a sum of ₹5,000 at 20% per annum compound interest, compounded annually, in 2 years, will be:", "options": [{"text": "₹6,563", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,247", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,760", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": "₹7,200"}, {"n": 9, "text": "The volume of a rectangular block of wood is 10,368 cm3. Its length, breadth and height are in the ratio of 3 : 2 : 1. If its entire surface is polished at ₹2/cm2, then find the total cost of polishing.", "options": [{"text": "₹6,336", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,135", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,436", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,356", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": "₹6,336"}, {"n": 10, "text": "Ravi bought a watch for ₹4,800, spent ₹200 on its repair, and sold it for ₹6,000. What is his profit percentage?", "options": [{"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "27%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "22%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "25"}, {"n": 11, "text": "₹8,200 is divided among A, B and C in such a way that if ₹19, ₹9 and ₹13 are deducted from their respective shares, they have money in the ratio 12:19:10. Find the difference between B’s and C’s original shares.", "options": [{"text": "₹1,787", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,841", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,691", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,641", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "₹1,787"}, {"n": 12, "text": "Two engines of trains 28 km apart start towards each other at speeds of 23 km/hr and 89 km/hr, respectively. After how much time will they meet each other? (Assume the length of engine is negligible)3620", "options": [{"text": "17 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "14 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "13 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "15 minutes", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": "15 minutes"}, {"n": 13, "text": "The sum of two numbers is 54 and their LCM is 195. The two numbers are:2609", "options": [{"text": "37, 17", "added": false}, {"text": "44, 10", "added": false}, {"text": "32, 22", "added": false}, {"text": "39, 15", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "39, 15"}, {"n": 14, "text": "In an election with two candidates, Candidate A received 75% of the total valid votes. If 10% of the total 14,000 votes were declared invalid, how many valid votes did Candidate B receive?", "options": [{"text": "3150", "added": false}, {"text": "4450", "added": false}, {"text": "3500", "added": false}, {"text": "3750", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "3150"}, {"n": 15, "text": "A, B and C together can complete a piece of work in 12 days, while A alone can complete it in 20 days and C alone can complete it in 36 days. In how many days can B alone complete the work?", "options": [{"text": "60 days", "added": false}, {"text": "180 days", "added": false}, {"text": "150 days", "added": false}, {"text": "120 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "180 days"}, {"n": 16, "text": "Three chairs and two tables together cost ₹600, two chairs and one table together cost ₹350. The cost of four chairs is:", "options": [{"text": "₹200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹400", "added": false}, {"text": "₹300", "added": false}, {"text": "₹100", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": "₹400"}, {"n": 17, "text": "Seven years ago from now, a man was five times as old as his son. Seven years from now, the father will be three times as old as his son. Find the son's present age.", "options": [{"text": "26 years", "added": false}, {"text": "38 years", "added": false}, {"text": "21 years", "added": false}, {"text": "31 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": "21 years"}, {"n": 18, "text": "In a quadrilateral QRST, ∠ Q = 74° and ∠ R = 39°. The bisectors of ∠ S and ∠ T meet at E. What is the measure of ∠ TES?", "options": [{"text": "47°", "added": false}, {"text": "43°", "added": false}, {"text": "56.5°", "added": false}, {"text": "61.5°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "quadrilaterals", "key_answer": "56.5°"}, {"n": 19, "text": "For 15 innings, a cricketer has an average of 94 runs. In the 16th inning, he scores 111 runs. His average score increased by _____. (Round off the answer to the nearest whole number.)980", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "1"}, {"n": 20, "text": "Sangeeta observes the top of a chimney at an angle of elevation of 45°. She is standing 28.7 metres away from the base of the chimney, and her eye level is 1.3 metres above the ground. What is the total height (in metres) of the chimney?", "options": [{"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "28.7", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "27.4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "heights-and-distances", "key_answer": "30"}, {"n": 21, "text": "If the listed price of a bag is 85% more than its cost price and a discount of 49% is announced on it, then find the loss percentage.", "options": [{"text": "9.31%", "added": false}, {"text": "9.12%", "added": false}, {"text": "5.65%", "added": false}, {"text": "5.42%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": "5.65%"}, {"n": 22, "text": "The number of prime numbers lying between 415 and 428 is:", "options": [{"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "types-of-numbers", "key_answer": "2"}]}